    "test_m2.py: The fake clock is set to 1000.0 only after the first call, while the first call recorded real time.time() (typically >>1000); subsequent calls therefore see a negative elapsed time and the entry is not expired, so the stale tests fail regardless of implementation. -> Patch the clock before the first call (e.g., 0.0, then 1000.0, then 1000.05) or set the patched time to time.time() + 1.",
    "test_m2.py: The tests patch the internal funcy.flow.time.time attribute, which is not a public API in the plan and may not exist under a valid implementation (e.g., `from time import time`). -> Use a public/stable clock injection or patch global time.time from before the first call; do not depend on module internals."
  ],
  "advisory": [
    "test_m2.py: The plan/milestone m2 explicitly includes `cache=cache` and an assertion that the explicit cache retains the refilled key_func-derived entry, but these tests never use or inspect an explicit cache, leaving that part of the behavior untested."
  ]
